CORE gcc-only
main.c
--no-standard-checks --arch x86_64 --os linux
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
When __builtin_va_list is modelled as void** (x86_64), a pointer to
the element type (va_tag*) passed to a function must be dereferenced
to obtain the va_list position, not used directly as a va_list.
The test pins --arch x86_64 --os linux because the va_list representation,
and hence the va_tag construction, is architecture specific.
Fixes: diffblue/cbmc#9176
